{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius","id":1124148,"title":"God Machine and the Clavicalvarius","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-02T20:29:24-07:00","id":1124148,"title":"God Machine and the Clavicalvarius","content":"So my current character concept is a Hippy Self-Help Therapist type who wants to enforce peacefulness on others through the use of Oneiromancy and Goetic magic. I see the Clavicalvaris mentioned in the new book but can't figure out what sort of Attainments they would have. I referenced the previous edition and I am thinking that At 1 would be like Know Nature + Emotional Urging and At 3 would probably be Goetic Summoning.... but 2 4 and 5 I am lost on. Maybe that is where spirit should come in and maybe something something something manipulating essence from emotions? I have no idea. The Oblations probably still work, and clearly the Keys of Solomon could be Yantra. But I dont have much direction for what to do with this new legacy system when it comes to interpreting existing Legacies or I guess even making my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T20:37:06-07:00","id":1124154,"title":"","content":"For clarity's sake, is the thread title meant to frame this as a question of &quot;How do I update the Clavicularius to the Second Edition/post-GMC mechanics?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T20:54:41-07:00","id":1124159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1124154#post1124154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarity's sake, is the thread title meant to frame this as a question of &quot;How do I update the Clavicularius to the Second Edition/post-GMC mechanics?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is what I was aiming for","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T20:59:54-07:00","id":1124162,"title":"","content":"Following up on lines like<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;The mage, having confronted her own </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Vice_(Storytelling_System)\" target=\"_blank\">Vices</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, feels qualified to confront the sins of everyone else.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I feel like At 1 Know Nature, At 2 Emotional Urging, At 3 Clear Thoughts, At 4 Goetic Summons, and maybe at 5 being like a bastardized Psychic Projection that allows your Goetia to beat up their goetia and act like some Psychic Reprogramming would be kind of neat but idk if it actually fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T06:45:30-07:00","id":1124279,"title":"","content":"So, this isn't about the Clavicularius and their interactions with the God-Machine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T17:28:27-07:00","id":1124541,"title":"","content":"Correct.... because they dont really have any direct interactions with the god machine exclusive to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:25:28-07:00","id":1124584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ResilientComma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1124541#post1124541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct.... because they dont really have any direct interactions with the god machine exclusive to them.</div> </div> </div> </div> That you know of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:24:03-07:00","id":1124757,"title":"","content":"remember guys that the Clavicularius are a Mastigos<b> Spirit</b> primary legacy their attainments should really grant spiritual effects with optional mind effects, my rough ideas would be:<br /> <br /> 1st attainment - exorcists eye, reach for advanced duration, - spend an hour in meditation upon your inner weaknesses, after reflecting on ones sins and vices the key-bearer can see the reflections of thier darker side in the world around them, For added character attainment doesn't unveil spiritual phenomena that resonate with positive emotion/resonance<br /> <br /> 2nd attainment - Know Spirit, reach for instant use and sensory range - once the Clavicularius can perceive the malign and destructive influence around them they can begin the road to understanding them, Added character - the attainment can bypass the Rank withstand if the targeted spirit matches the users vice, self examination is the most rewarding and enlightening<br /> <br /> 3rd attainment - Ephemeral Shield, reach for advanced duration, also protects against spirits physical attacks, once the Clavicularius understands their failings they can shut off the influence they have upon them, spend an hour ritually girding yourself from weakness, the attainment automatically gains (spirit dots) in successes to contest any clash of wills. For added character attainment doesn't protect against spiritual phenomena that resonate with positive emotion/resonance<br /> <br /> 4th attainment - Command Spirit, Instant use, Sensory range, advanced duration - can instantly command a spirit you can see to undertake (spirit dots) actions within the duration, automatically scores (spirit dots) in any clash made by the spirit trying to resist Added character - the attainment can bypass the Rank withstand if the targeted spirit matches the users vice<br /> <br /> <i>not massively happy with the fifth attainment, would have liked to keep the old create fetish power but i dont see it as being feasibly useful using the new legacy creation guidelines, but anyhow:</i><br /> <br /> 5th attainment - World Walker, instant use, sensory range - previously demonstrated command over the spirit and exerted dominance the willworker can now simply banish the spirit from their presence, sending them hurtling back onto the other side of the gauntlet. <br /> <br /> now just to add some mind optional bits ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:04:39-07:00","id":1124799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1124757#post1124757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">remember guys that the Clavicularius are a Mastigos<b> Spirit</b> primary legacy their attainments should really grant spiritual effects with optional mind effects, my rough ideas would be:</div> </div> </div> </div>You are thinking the Bene Ashmadi, their cousin. The Clavicalvarius is mind Primary with Spirit Secondary. The original legacy didn't even have spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:09:15-07:00","id":1124801,"title":"","content":"nope both legacies are listed together in the Other Legacies section as Mastigos legacies with Spirit as a ruling arcana,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:13:58-07:00","id":1124803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1124801#post1124801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nope both legacies are listed together in the Other Legacies section as Mastigos legacies with Spirit as a ruling arcana,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is good and all except I am also reading the original legacy literally right now. Though I do have to correct myself, they do use spirit on their last attainment<br /> <br /> Goetic Projection: Gnosis 3, Mind 2, Empathy 3<br /> Goetic Bulwark: Gnosis 5, Mind 3<br /> The Binding Seal: Gnosis 7, Mind 4, Spirit 4, Empathy 4<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:25:59-07:00","id":1124877,"title":"","content":"Yes, we changed it so they were a Mastigos Legacy with Spirit Primary.<br /> <br /> (Because summoning Goetia and giving them Manifestations relies on Spirit (or Death) more than it did last edition)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:39:05-07:00","id":1124892,"title":"","content":"Surely if they get a second edition revamp you could just call them Goetics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:40:58-07:00","id":1124893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1124877#post1124877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, we changed it so they were a Mastigos Legacy with Spirit Primary.<br /> <br /> (Because summoning Goetia and giving them Manifestations relies on Spirit (or Death) more than it did last edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>So why not use Death then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:08:17-07:00","id":1124964,"title":"","content":"The clavulcalarius see themselves as the spiritual (pun intended) successors to the biblical king Solomon, who was rewarded by god for his humility and wisdom with power over demons and spirits. The Legacy use thier ability to overcome thier own character flaws as credence to pass judgement on the failings and flaws of others. spirit just plain makes more sense than death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:18:59-07:00","id":1124966,"title":"","content":"I just wrote up a 2e version of the Clavicularii for a char I intend to play. Not sure if Attainments 2 and 3 shouldn't be swapped, but it made more sense to me this way around. The legacy has changed a bit here, but I think I managed to stay with the original themes. No emotional urging, simply didn't find a good spot to put it into. The legacy now begins with self knowledge (was present in 1e), masterin of the self (also 1e) and warding off spirits/goetia (not in 1e). At higher level spirits/goetia are being summoned, fetiches created (which admittedly only works with low ranking goetia due to the rules. But if are a gnosis 6 Clavicularius and your inner demons are Rank 3 or higher you either walk a very dangerous path or a loosing the battle) and (inner) demons banished.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i><b>Clavicularius</b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I didn't want to copy too much out of Legacies the Sublime... thus the empty spaces</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Parentage:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Mastigos, Silver Ladder</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Nickname: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Solomonists or Key-Bearers</span><br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> <b>Appearances:</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: Mind 2, Willpower 5, two dots in one of the following Skills; Academics, Occult, Empathy, Expression or Persuasion</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Initiation</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Organization</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Theory</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ruling Arcanum</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: Mind</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Yantras</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">: Spell is thematically related to a Goetic demon the mage subjugated within the past month, resisting a vice, using the keys of Solomon, utilizing the subjects Virtue or Vice. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Oblations</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Rite of Castigation. Meditation on past moments of weakness. Engaging in psychological therapy (either as the therapist or as a patient). Scribing the Keys of Solomon in a durable medium (such as stone, metal or enamel).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>First: Goetic Awareness<br /> Prerequisites: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Initiation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">To master demons of any kind, one needs to be aware of their presence first. Through this attainment the Key-Bearer the Key-Bearer becomes aware of Spirits in his vincinity. This Attainment emulates &quot;Exorcist's Eyes&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. If the Solomonists possesses Mind 1, the effects of this Attainment also extend to Goetia.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"> Mind 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Solomonists know their demons and those of others. Whenever someone they perceive fulfills his Virtue or Vice the mage can feel the powerful demons of the person stir. This Attainment emulates &quot;Witness&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Second: Goetic Bulwark</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 2,</span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Willpower 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">The Clavicularii know that to defeat an overwhelming foe you first have to take away the source of their strength. Thus they learn to ward those things in the phenomenal world that give demons strength by inscribing marking them with the Solomonic seals. This Attainment replicates &quot;Cap the Well&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"> Mind 2 </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Solomonists learn to discipline their own minds and tame their own demons. When tempted by his Vice a Key-Bearer may choose to wrestle the Goetic demon of his Vice for control. The player rolls Resolve + Composure and compares the result to the mages Mind dots. If he scored more successes he is overwhelmed by his Goetic demon and thus has to indulge in his vice. Doing so does not replenish a willpower point. If the mages Mind dots equal or exceed the successes of the roll the mage forces his own demon into submission. He does not indulge in the Vice but still regains a willpower point as if he had fulfilled his Vice.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Third: Goetic Shield</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 3, the Key-Bearer must </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">The Solomonist rises above and beyond the influence of demons. The powers of spiritual entities fail when faced with the Key-Bearers determination and enlightened soul. This Attainment emulates &quot;Ephemeral Shield&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and to include the physical attacks of Spirits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\"> Mind 3<br /> <br /> The benefits of this Attainment extend to Goetia and any affects that target the Solomonists mind, emulating &quot;Mental Shield&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and to include the physical attacks of Goetia.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Fourth: Goetic Subjugation</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 4,</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Willpower 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Clavicularius binds demons to his will. By inscribing the Solomonic seals onto an object and then ritually forcing a vanquished spirit into the item he creates a Fetish. This Attainment emulates &quot;Craft Fetish&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. If the Solomonists has Mind 4, this Attainment may be used on Goetia aswell as on Spirits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Optional:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Key-Bearer learns to call forth his inner demons by the force of his will, forcing them to attend the Solomonists call and take on physical form. This emulates &quot;Goetic Summons&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and to Summoning a Goetia from the mages own Oneiros. By adding in Spirit 2, the Spirit gains the Materialized Condition for the duration of the summons. Subjugating the Goetic demon to the mages will is another matter...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Fifth: Goetic Banishment</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Prerequisites: </b></span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Spirit 5,</span><span style=\"color:#231f20\">the Key-Bearer must </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 4, or must attain three dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements, or two dots in a third Skill from the list.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Clavicularius can ban demons from his presence. With but a gesture invoking one of the Solomonic Keys he can banish the demon from the material plane. This Attainment emulates &quot;Banishment&quot; with Reach assigned to Instand Casting and Sensory Range. If the mage also has Mind 4 this Attainment may be used on Goetia aswell as on Spirits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Optional: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mind 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">As he can banish spirits without himself, the mage can vanquish his own demons for a short time. Though many Solomonists don't like to admit it, this Attainment can be used to purge the Key-Bearer of Virtue, just as it can battle Vice. This Attainment emulates &quot;Amorality&quot; with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#231f20\">New Spell:</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Witness (Mind </b></span><span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Practice: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Unveiling</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Primary Factor: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Empathy, Science, Subterfuge<br /> To the subject people wear their hearts on their sleeves. Whenever someone he perceives acts on his Virtue or Vice the subject becomes aware of this fact.<br /> </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:54:18-07:00","id":1125046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1124877#post1124877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, we changed it so they were a Mastigos Legacy with Spirit Primary.<br /> <br /> (Because summoning Goetia and giving them Manifestations relies on Spirit (or Death) more than it did last edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>But summoning is purely Mind when it comes to Goetia, and adding Manifestations is not useful (if it's even possible) before summoning them. So Spirit primary still seems backwards to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T19:52:09-07:00","id":1125059,"title":"","content":"Mastigos has Mind. But can learn Spirit. When joining the Legacy, Spirit becomes your third Primary Arcana, letting you get and cast it cheaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:00:51-07:00","id":1125060,"title":"","content":"To be fair it still feels backwards for their Attainments to use Spirit as the primary Arcanum. It definitly makes sense to make it this way around to unlock the additional ruling Arcanum for it's predominantly Mastigos practitioners, but it's probably feel more intuitive if it was Mind primary, Spirit secondary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:36:08-07:00","id":1125092,"title":"","content":"Honestly I kinda agree with some of whats being said, <br /> <br /> The the legacy section, the Eleventh Question and the Nagaraja write ups clearly show that it is intended that legacy attainments are supposed to be primarily based of the ruling arcana granted by the legacy with supplemental effects depending on one optional arcana drawn from the legacies parent path. This is not however anywhere that I can see explicitly stated. So although I believe this is certainly Rule-as-Intended it may not be Rule-as-Written, not saying RAW is better for the game than RAI just that it could be interpenetrated that way.<br /> <br /> That being say it does seem weird that the Goetic aspect of the Clavicularius ends up as &quot;optional&quot; when you follow what seems to be the intended way of constructing a 2e legacy. <br /> <br /> For what its worth should the Dev Gods deem it worthy, I'd love to see a legacy write up who either doesn't grant a new ruling arcana, or who's attainments are primarily based off their path arcana not the new ruling arcana, just so we'd have a template for how that's supposed to look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T22:48:37-07:00","id":1125110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1124877#post1124877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, we changed it so they were a Mastigos Legacy with Spirit Primary.<br /> <br /> (Because summoning Goetia and giving them Manifestations relies on Spirit (or Death) more than it did last edition)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the clarification. Its nice to have a dev weigh in. I am probably going to go ahead and do some rewrite on it now that I know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:17:34-07:00","id":1125156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1124148-god-machine-and-the-clavicalvarius?p=1125059#post1125059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mastigos has Mind. But can learn Spirit. When joining the Legacy, Spirit becomes your third Primary Arcana, letting you get and cast it cheaper.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes more sense but it's kinda iffy due to being a completely meta and gamey way of deciding what should be the primary Arcanum.<br /> And I'll admit that I tend to forget that adding the secondary Arcanum as Ruling if the primary already is Ruling is just a houserule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}